  "final": "Change complete and verified.\n\n## What changed\n\n**New shared module — `src/money.ts`**\n- Exports `formatAmount(cents: number): string` with the exact arithmetic both old helpers used: `-` sign for negatives, whole units via `Math.floor(absolute / 100)`, and fraction digits via `String(absolute % 100).padStart(2, '0')`. No rounding change, no currency symbol (e.g. `123 → '1.23'`, `0 → '0.00'`, `-1 → '-0.01'`).\n\n**Migrated renderers (single change, public interfaces untouched)**\n- `src/invoice.ts`: imports `formatAmount` from `./money`; `renderInvoice(id, cents)` still prepends the `$` itself, so its interface and output are unchanged.\n- `src/report.ts`: imports `formatAmount` from `./money`; `renderReport(rows)` keeps its row shape, comma format, and line order.\n\n**Removed old API**\n- Deleted `src/invoiceAmount.ts` and `src/reportAmount.ts` (the sanctioned \"delete\" option), so `invoiceAmount`/`reportAmount` no longer exist anywhere in `src/` — verified by grep. There were no other callers.\n\n**Checks extended (`checks/public.cjs`)**\n- Original assertions kept verbatim; added coverage for `formatAmount` directly (positive/zero/negative/hundred boundary) and for both renderers across positive, zero, and negative cents, including a multi-row report confirming output and line order (`'p,1.23\\nz,0.00\\nn,-1.25\\nw,1.00'`).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tsc -p tsconfig.json` — clean compile of `src/` (emits `.build/{invoice,money,report}.js`); the deleted helper modules no longer compile.\n- `node checks/public.cjs` — all original and added assertions pass.\n\nBehavior is byte-for-byte identical to before for both renderers; only the duplicated conversion logic was consolidated.",
